  "question": {
    "text": "In the circuit shown, what will be the current through the $6 \\mathrm{V}$ zener? <img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/2019_phy_q5.png\">",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "4cOvx",
      "text": "$6 \\mathrm{mA}$, from $\\mathrm{A}$ to $\\mathrm{B}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "5IKR0",
      "text": "$2 \\mathrm{mA},$ from $\\mathrm{A}$ to $\\mathrm{B}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "jo2NV",
      "text": "$2 \\mathrm{mA},$ from $B$ to $\\mathrm{A}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "eUUy9",
      "text": "Zero",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "According to the question\r\nInput voltage $V_{s}=10 \\mathrm{V}$ \r\nSource resistance $R_{S}=1 \\mathrm{k} \\Omega$ \r\nZener diode voltage $V_{Z}=6 \\mathrm{V}$\r\n$\\because$ Breakdown voltage of zener diode is $=6 \\mathrm{V},$ and the potential difference across the zener diode $5 \\mathrm{V}$.\r\n$\\therefore$ Current flow in zener diode $I_{z}=0$\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/2019_phy_a5.png\">",
    "image": null
  },
